		<td width="150" align="left" valign="top" class="row1"><span class="name"><a name="37142"></a><b>Guest</b></span><br /><span class="postdetails"><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /></span><br /></td>
		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=37142&amp;sid=c35cc850287ece723ee443e0ea5b056e#37142"><img src="templates/subBlack/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Sat Oct 09, 2004 5:58 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=37142&amp;sid=c35cc850287ece723ee443e0ea5b056e"><img src="templates/subBlack/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">I knew Sor from trialing in DR and a little before then, i always had known her and Pars to be the dearest of people, always there to help, welcoming you warmly whenever in their presence. I cannot describe how badly i feel to hear about this, i am sitting at my computer with tears in my eyes and a lump in my throat. Pars if you ever need to talk about it, you know i am always willing to listen, my e-mail address is <a href="mailto:reelbiggoldmx@hotmail.com">reelbiggoldmx@hotmail.com</a> 
<br />

<br />
Sor will be missed so much, i truly believe that in heaven she will spread her warmth, looking down and blessing us all.
<br />

<br />
I know its hard to do Pars but keep your chin up, be the strong person that i know you to be and i know Sors family will appreciate you being there for them.
<br />

<br />
Doio/James</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
			</tr>
