			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">So sorry to hear of the loss of Soraea
<br />

<br />
This may or not comfort in any way but heard this anon poem a long time ago and hope it will uplift in times of great sorrow.
<br />

<br />
Do not stand at my grave and weep,
<br />
I am not there, I do not sleep,
<br />
I am a thousand winds that blow, 
<br />
I am the diamond glints in snow,
<br />
I am the sumlight on ripened grain, 
<br />
I am the gentle autumn rain.
<br />

<br />
When you awaken in the morning hush,
<br />
I am the uplifting rush 
<br />
of quiet birds in circled flight,
<br />
I am the soft stars that shine at night,
<br />
Do not stand at my grave and cry, 
<br />
I am not there, I did not die.
<br />
                            
<br />

<br />
Whazzoom
<br />
member of Sovereign Crusaders</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
